I'm currently considering to port the Go (cf. http://golang.org/)
runtime library included in GCC 4.6 to Tru64 UNIX V5.1.  One issue that
came up is the need for a object file section to store language-specific
data.  On ELF systems, this is easy since you can have arbitrary named
sections.  In ECOFF, there's the .comment section that seem to fit the
bill.  They are described in much detail in

	http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51B_HTML/SUPPDOCS/OBJSPEC/TITLE.HTM

but unfortunately the Assembly Language Programmer's Guide doesn't give
any indication on how to create at the assembler level.  While strings
on /usr/ccs/lib/cmplrs/cc/{adu, as[01]} indicates that there is support,
I've not been able to determine the syntax.

Any help would be appreciated.

Thanks.
	Rainer

